          "c": "你今晚得閒嗎？",
          "j": "nei5 gam1 maan5 dak1 haan4 maa3?",
          "e": "Are you free tonight?",
          "note": "得閒 (dak1 haan4) is the Cantonese for \"free / having spare time\" — 你今晚得閒嗎？(nei5 gam1 maan5 dak1 haan4 maa3?) \"are you free tonight?\". Its opposite is 唔得閒 (m4 dak1 haan4) \"busy\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "你",
              "j": "nei5",
              "e": "you"
            },
            {
              "c": "今晚",
              "j": "gam1 maan5",
              "e": "tonight"
            },
            {
              "c": "得閒",
              "j": "dak1 haan4",
              "e": "free"
            },
            {
              "c": "嗎",
              "j": "maa3",
              "e": "(yes/no)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "friends-t1-s03",
          "c": "我哋一齊出街啦！",
          "j": "ngo5 dei6 jat1 cai4 ceot1 gaai1 laa1!",
          "e": "Let's go out together!",
          "note": "出街 (ceot1 gaai1), literally \"out to the street\", is the Cantonese for \"go out / head into town\" — 一齊出街 (jat1 cai4 ceot1 gaai1) \"let's go out together\". 一齊 (jat1 cai4) is \"together\".",
          "bd": [
